<title>UK: UK Jan oil output down 54,000 bpd to 2.686 mln - APR.</title>
<headline>UK Jan oil output down 54,000 bpd to 2.686 mln - APR.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British oil production fell slightly in January, down 54,429 barrels a day (bpd) to 2,686,242 bpd from 2,740,671 million in December, Aberdeen Petroleum Report (APR) said.</p>
<p>Extra production from the Alba field, boosted to 98,994 bpd by a second phase of development, was outweighed by slippage from other fields.</p>
<p>Nelson output, part of the Forties stream, fell almost 50,000 bpd to 136,650 bpd.</p>
<p>Brent output was down 10,000 bpd at 182,000 bpd.</p>
<p>Scott rose 20,000 bpd to 184,000 bpd.</p>
<p>--Richard Mably, London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
</text>
